THOUGHT: The staged checks cover a large surface, so I’ll implement a compact standard-library service around shared SQLite WAL state, with per-node HTTP servers, a real supervised Redis listener set, durable channel event rows, polling-based WebSocket fanout/replay, IRC bridging, and a selector-complete SPA. This establishes the executable foundation quickly for iterative checks.

